BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:[Stanford University Libraries] Text Machines: Scarlet Thread of t
 he Digital Order (1883-2026)
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260912
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260912
DTSTAMP:20260911T165617Z
UID:stanford_campus-localist-53251159287291-53251159382627@local-events
DESCRIPTION:Stanford Libraries now holds an 1883 edition of a rare book\,
  Les laboureurs: poème tiré de Jocelyn\, whose pages (text and ornamen
 ts) were entirely woven on a Jacquard loom by the firm of silk merchant Jo
 seph-Alphonse Henry. This exhibition explores the cultural contexts and ma
 terial conditions of Les laboureurs’ production\, and considers parall
 els between technology-driven global change in the late nineteenth century
  and in our current day. The exhibition includes microscope images reveali
 ng the\n\nAges: All ages\nLast synced: 2026-09-11 09:56 PDT
LOCATION:Green Library\, Bing Wing
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:[Stanford Center for Continuing Medical Education] MRI: Clinical U
 pdates and Practical Physics
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260912T072000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260912T180000
DTSTAMP:20260911T165617Z
UID:stanford_campus-localist-50852323821947-50852323822972@local-events
DESCRIPTION:OverviewThis activity is a 4-day course for practicing Radiolo
 gists and Magnetic Resonance technologists. The conference will focus on n
 ew strategies to correctly interpret common MRI exams\, recognize image qu
 ality issues\, and execute strategies to correct them. In addition\, this 
 course will review the underlying principles of MR physics and image proto
 col decisions with colleagues to improve team efficiency.\n\nRegistration
 \nRegistration fees includes course materials\, certificate of participati
 on\n\nAges: All ages\nSource: https://stanford.cloud-cme.com/course/course
 overview?P=5&EID=55765\nLast synced: 2026-09-11 09:56 PDT
LOCATION:The Frances C. Arrillaga Alumni Center\, Stanford\, CA
URL:https://stanford.cloud-cme.com/course/courseoverview?P=5&EID=55765
END:VEVENT
