BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:[Bioengineering] PhD Dissertation Defense: Eliel Akinbami
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260915T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260915T140000
DTSTAMP:20260911T165617Z
UID:stanford_campus-localist-53933108327942-53933108328967@local-events
DESCRIPTION:Title: Reading Enzyme Function from Sequence and Structure\n\n
 Abstract: Enzymes are among the most proficient catalysts known – the ba
 cterial phosphatase PafA\, for example\, accelerates its reaction by rough
 ly 1027-fold relative to the uncatalyzed reaction. Yet how a linear amino-
 acid sequence folds into a structure that achieves this\, and how mutation
 s to individual residues tune catalytic activity\, is still only partly un
